# Monorepo root ignores. Each project (backend/, mobile/) has its own .gitignore too.

# Dependencies (also ignored per-project, listed here as a backstop)
**/node_modules/
backend/vendor/

# Environment
**/.env
!**/.env.example

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.log

# Build output
mobile/www/
mobile/dist/
mobile/.angular/

# NOTE: mobile/android and mobile/ios are deliberately NOT ignored. They were, until the first
# on-device pass needed a manifest change (debug-only cleartext, so a native build can reach a local
# API) and regeneration destroyed it. The native projects are not build output: they hold
# app-specific configuration that has nowhere else to live — the manifest, icons, signing config and
# plugin registrations. Their own .gitignore (generated by `cap add`) already excludes the parts that
# ARE build output: build/, .gradle/, local.properties, the copied web assets and generated config.
